===Etymology===
{{compound|en|touch|stone}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtʌt͡ʃstəʊn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[stone]] used to check the quality of [[gold]] [[alloys]] by rubbing them to leave a visible trace. [[Category:en:Gold]]
# {{lb|en|figurative|by extension}} A standard of [[comparison]] or [[evaluation]].
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=The foregoing doctrine affords us also a '''touchstone''' for the trial of spirits.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Ann Baynes Coiro|author2=Thomas Fulton|title=Rethinking Historicism from Shakespeare to Milton|page=243
|passage=In the print firestorm that followed the publication of the royal couple's letters, the generalissima was one polemical '''touchstone'''. The Annotations to ''The Kings Cabinet Opened'' itself depicted the queen as an enemy to king and country: {{...}}}}

